00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:11.750
"An eerie swelling of unknown origins
constricted around my heart!

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.790
Was it frustration or disgust?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.460
It felt like a hangover after drinking,

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.930
but one that came
from drinking every day."

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:24.720
That's unexpected! He's the type
that reads with passion!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.720
"That's how it felt; and it was bad."

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:30.430
This Amihama... I think he's the type
that gives everything 100%.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.650
Really? "The Mask"?

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:38.650
But if he gives everything 100%,
why did he quit swimming?

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.940
True...

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.360
Maybe he burned out.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.360
Hmm?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.370
I talked to the guy who knows about him.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.910
Apparently, Amihama joined
swimming to beat his big brother.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:51.960
His brother?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:57.040
So, once he beat his brother,
he had no reason to swim?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.630
Pro'ly.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.590
It'll be tough to get him back into it.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.260
Um...

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.970
Hmm?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.810
Never mind. It's nothing.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.480
Say it. We're all ears.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.810
Mmm.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:20.440
What if we helped Amihama
find a reason to swim again?

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.860
Hmm?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.780
Let's give him reasons to swim.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.360
Library

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.380
Wow, I had no idea!

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:39.590
Water polo sounds great to get fit!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.920
It's more than swimming.
You jump and shoot, too.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.890
It works out a bunch of muscles.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:51.140
Well, maybe I'll join water polo, then!

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.230
What a killer body!
Nothing beats looking buff!

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:06.780
Y-Yeah. He's on Poseidon Japan,
the national water polo team.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.200
So if I join, I can get
a buff body like that?!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:13.490
Step Closer

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.790
Well, it'll take work.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:16.540
Maybe I'll give water polo a shot!

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.040
Sounds fun, right?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.500
Yeah!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.590
"Kendo Club"
"Martial Arts Hall"
"This Way!"
"Beginners Welcome!!"

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.020
Um, where's the ball?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.100
Huh? What?! Amihama?!

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.610
We were just doing some passing practice!

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.150
Huh? You're surprised we
practice water polo on land?

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:49.410
Yup! Don't we love passing
the ball, Captain?

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.910
Oh! If it isn't Amihyama!
I'm the captain--

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.250
What is it this time?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.460
Huh?

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:01.590
Just say it. If I join water polo,
what good things will happen?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:09.840
Oh, sure! There's a lot, but I like
forming deep bonds with my teammates!

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.720
Teammates?

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:17.350
Yeah! It's all about teamwork!
Teammates unleash your full potential!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:18.850
That's enough.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.690
Huh?

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:26.610
You thought this would make me join?
Quite the opposite--I'm appalled.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:34.030
If any of your awkward friends are out
there, stop listening and come out.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.000
I knew it.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.460
What gives, Ushi?! You said he'd see
the appeal of water polo and join!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.380
Sorry.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.210
Now, now, now...

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.880
The redhead's poor acting
appalled me the most.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.970
Eh?!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.970
What was wrong with it?!

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.470
I've gotta agree with him.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:01.100
"What a killer body!
Nothing beats looking buff!"

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.730
I wasn't like that!

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.110
You were.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.360
That sounds awful.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:08.900
Yours was, too.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:09.900
Eh?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.120
That double take was ridiculous.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.660
Yeah, that was strange one.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.580
You're the one who screwed up his name!

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.830
Shuddap! I was nervous!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.790
So much for your "bond forming."

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:30.010
Stop with this nonsense. I won't join.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.800
Please! We need your speed!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:35.680
No.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.720
I'm begging you!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.730
Can you please stop?

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.140
I won't.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.640
How can I make you?

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.360
I said, "I won't!"

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.650
Are you dumb?

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:53.660
Yup! We're dumb! We'll keep pestering you
'cuz we don't know any better!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.290
Then I'll keep saying it:
"I don't want to swim."

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.330
No use, huh?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.330
May I say something?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.580
Hmm?

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.960
To be honest, I'm not athletic at all.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.380
Really?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:16.140
I'm no good at sports,
but I am pretty tall.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:22.060
Everyone expects a lot from me,
but I'm never any good.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:25.900
It's tough letting everyone down.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:32.950
Just yesterday, my classmates dragged
me along, saying I'd be good at it.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.700
That's when I met Minato.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:43.160
He was a water polo star, but he got in
an accident and forgot all about it.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:49.090
He said the high expectations
are tough, and not to rely on him.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:54.800
I understand those feelings
so much that it hurts.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.760
I was unsure about water polo,
but Minato convinced me.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.480
I could see myself playing
with someone like him.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.480
So that's what he meant...

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:14.650
When people like me with no talent
see gifted people like you not using it,

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.780
it feels like such a waste.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:25.120
You say you have no reason to swim,
but isn't having the gift reason enough?

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:31.420
Whoa! Babayaro with some moving words!
Maybe they'll reach his heart!

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:32.840
Let's swim.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.470
Hooked 'em!

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.430
Nice, Babi!

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.930
You really will?!

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:43.060
Yes. We'll have a race
where I'll join if you win,

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:46.190
but if you lose, leave me alone.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.730
Huh?

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.060
What?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:53.190
I'll get fed up if you
pester me every single day.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:12:02.410
Make it 150 meters. I'll swim solo, but
you can do a six-person 25-meter relay.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.830
You're kidding me. Even with six...

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:11.710
Didn't you say that teammates
unleash your full potential?

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.550
What now?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:18.800
Shit! That was just me imagining
having teammates.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.350
I wouldn't know 'cuz I've never had any!

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:25.220
Now's not the time to admit that!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.770
Question! What's your 100-meter PR?

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.150
52.77.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:33.480
Is that slow?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.860
So fast, it's funny.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.650
The hell?!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:40.410
So, you'd like to forfeit instead of race?

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.120
Argh!

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.580
Like hell we would!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.790
We'll never just give up without a fight!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.080
But, give us a hendy!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.040
Huh?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.630
Hmm?

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.460
Say again?

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:03.300
I said, we'll never just give up
without a fight!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.520
But, give us a handicap!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.480
Pathetic.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:11.350
We stand no chance without one!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:16.860
These three have hardly ever swum,
let alone played water polo.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.360
If we lose, we'll stop for good. Please!

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.780
Promise?

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.320
Y-Yeah!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:29.080
Then, I'll give you a
20-second head start.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:32.370
The showdown's on Friday. Three days.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.290
Eh?

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.880
Not today?!

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.880
I already have plans to
try out the other clubs.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:47.060
To start off, we'll time
our swimming speeds.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.520
I wonder how fast they are.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:53.730
Speaking of which,
I wonder how fast I am...

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:06.950
Sorry I'm slow!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.370
Don't worry!

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.620
Nice effort!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.210
Good work!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.330
Last up, Minato-<i>senpai</i>.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.630
Uh, right.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.510
Ready!

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.550
Whoa! Nice form!

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.300
Wow!

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.270
Nice and hot!

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.980
Feels good!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.320
Mmm.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:43.360
Hmm? Why the smirk?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:49.740
Uh, I'm just surprised how fast I am
compared to my memories from 6th grade.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.750
Yeah? Well, you're bigger and stronger--

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:57.710
No! That wasn't even close!
You're way faster!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.210
Y-Yeah?

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.760
We won't beat Amihama unless we're faster!

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:06.680
His PR of 52:77 is for 100 meters.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:11.970
Multiplying by 1.5 gives 1:19
for 150 meters.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.890
With a 20-second handicap, that's 1:39.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:21.780
In comparison, I did 25 meters in 13:90.
Captain was 14:70.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:25.650
Minato was 16:10. Ejiri was 16:30.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:32.080
Babayaro did 20:20, and Ushimado,
30 flat, for a total of 1:51:20.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.750
Even with a handicap,
we lose by 12 seconds.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:40.290
As it is, there's no way we'll beat him.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:47.090
But there're six of us.
Cut two seconds each and we might.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.760
Sweet!

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:56.140
However, it won't be easy for me
and Captain to cut off two seconds.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.480
Let's focus on you four.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.570
Do you think it's possible?

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:07.700
Babayaro and Ushimado can work on diving.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.280
A good dive can cut a second or two.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.580
Okay!

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:17.460
Ejiri relies on power too much,
so we'll address his form.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:20.420
My form, huh? Sure.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:27.340
Minato just needs to swim more.
Before, you might have swum a 12.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:31.970
Getting close to your old speed
will be the key to winning.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.390
Right.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:41.060
Twelve seconds, huh?
I must've been pretty awesome.

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:50.070
If my memories return, will I go back to
being as awesome as I used to be?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.410
Hmm? That sound...

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.700
Has it started?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.500
It's just like before!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.870
Yup!

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.680
More finesse!

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.640
Less flopping around!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.720
Wait!

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:58.520
Big bro! Wait!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.900
Morning.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.070
Morning. Your bento is done.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:17.740
I open a bento I made for myself.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:24.120
Even though I know what's inside,
I pretend to be surprised.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:31.090
I'm used to this sort of life--
a life without a mother or brother.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:34.300
A life without swimming.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:39.850
Today, I swim so I never
have to swim again.

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:51.240
It's finally time. We've gotta win!

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:06.170
Five seconds! Four! Three! Two! One! Go!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.880
Go! Go! Go!

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:12.590
First up is Eitaro,
followed by Captain and Ejiri--

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:16.640
our fastest swimmers first
to make Amihama panic.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.790
So fast!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.500
How's that?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:55.880
Not good enough. His focus
on form is killing his speed.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.130
Look!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.480
Crap! Crap! Crap!

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.230
So fast!

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.750
Yes!

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:32.340
--Go! Go, Babi!
--Go! C'mon, Babi!

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:37.010
Go! Go! Go!

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:46.310
Go!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.730
Show 'em, Ushi!

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:01.660
He's catching up!

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:05.120
We're counting on you, Minato-<i>senpai</i>.

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:08.790
Leave it to me. I feel like I've got this!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.970
Ah, this feels good!

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:23.800
I'm flying through the water!

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:28.230
I had no idea I could swim this fast!

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:34.650
Awesome! Yes! Now we can start
playing water polo together!

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.240
Uh...

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.790
Yes!
